* Semantic Networks

- @Definition@: **Semantic Networks** represent knowledge as graphs of concepts
  and relations
  - E.g., WordNet, ConceptNet

::: columns
:::: {.column width=50%}

- @Components@:
  - _Nodes_: concepts (entities)
  - _Edges_: semantic relations
    - E.g., "is-a", "part-of", "has-property"

- @Pros@:
  - Easy to visualize and traverse
  - Support reasoning via path traversal
  - Used in early AI and current KGs

::::
:::: {.column width=50%}

// TODO(ai_gp): Apply the style from graphviz.rules.md
```graphviz
digraph SemanticNetwork {
    rankdir=TB;
    node [shape=ellipse, style=filled, fontname=Helvetica];
    edge [fontname=Helvetica];

    animal [label="Animal", fillcolor="#C6A6F4"];
    dog [label="Dog", fillcolor="#A0D6D1"];
